# Plan: "Now Playing" overlay card on the map

## Context

Today the only "now playing" surface is a Leaflet popup on the album marker (`AlbumBubble.jsx`). The user wants a persistent, Spotify-dark-theme control card pinned to the **top-right corner** of the window, sitting above the map, showing artwork, track name, artist(s), the artist's place of origin, a read-only progress bar, and **play/pause + next** controls.

Adding real playback controls requires two things the app doesn't have yet:
1. The `user-modify-playback-state` OAuth scope (current scope is read-only `user-read-currently-playing`). **Existing tokens will lack it — users must re-login after this change.**
2. Player fields (`is_playing`, `progress_ms`, `duration_ms`, all artists) that `fetchCurrentlyPlaying` currently fetches but discards.

Design decisions confirmed with the author:
- **Progress bar:** smooth client-side interpolation — anchor on `progress_ms` + a receive-timestamp, tick a ~500ms local timer forward while `is_playing`, clamp to `duration_ms`, re-anchor on each 5s poll.
- **Control failures** (403 non-Premium/restricted, 404 no active device): show a subtle generic "feature not available" hint on the card, don't crash.

## Approach

### 1. `src/spotify.js` — scope, widened fetch, control functions

**Scope** (`spotify.js:5`) — add only the minimum needed (per `docs/spotify-api-guidelines.md` rule on minimal scopes). Space-separated string:
```js
const SCOPE = "user-read-currently-playing user-modify-playback-state";
```
`URLSearchParams` encodes the space as `+`; `buildAuthUrl` needs no other change.

**Widen `fetchCurrentlyPlaying` return** (`spotify.js:36-40`). Keep `artistName` as the **primary** artist so the existing geo lookup and `lastArtistRef` comparison in `MapView` keep working; add a joined display string and the player fields:
```js
return {
  trackName: data.item.name,
  artistName: data.item.artists[0]?.name ?? null,        // primary — geo lookup key
  artistNames: data.item.artists.map((a) => a.name).join(", ") || null, // display
  albumImageUrl: data.item.album.images[0]?.url ?? null,
  trackId: data.item.id,
  isPlaying: data.is_playing,
  progressMs: data.progress_ms,
  durationMs: data.item.duration_ms,
};
```

**New control functions.** Confirm endpoint paths against the Spotify OpenAPI spec (guidelines rule — don't guess), then add a shared helper that mirrors the existing error handling (`spotify.js:25-31`), treating **204 as success** and surfacing the control-specific failures:
```js
async function playerCommand(method, command, token) {
  const response = await fetch(`https://api.spotify.com/v1/me/player/${command}`, {
    method,
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` },
  });
  if (response.status === 204) return;                       // success (no body)
  if (response.status === 401) throw new Error("TOKEN_EXPIRED");
  if (response.status === 403) throw new Error("PLAYBACK_UNAVAILABLE"); // non-Premium/restricted
  if (response.status === 404) throw new Error("NO_ACTIVE_DEVICE");
  if (response.status === 429) {
    const retryAfter = response.headers.get("Retry-After") ?? "5";
    throw new Error(`RATE_LIMITED:${retryAfter}`);
  }
  if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`SPOTIFY_ERROR:${response.status}`);
}

export const play       = (token) => playerCommand("PUT",  "play", token);
export const pause      = (token) => playerCommand("PUT",  "pause", token);
export const skipToNext = (token) => playerCommand("POST", "next", token);
```

### 2. `src/components/NowPlayingCard.jsx` — new component

Self-contained, inline-styled (matches the repo's no-CSS-file convention — see `LoginButton.jsx`, `MapView.jsx:89-116`). Fixed top-right, `zIndex: 1000` (above Leaflet's ~800 controls; top-right also avoids the top-left zoom buttons).

**Props:** `track` (widened object above), `placeName` (string), `onPlayPause`, `onNext`, `controlMessage` (string|null).

**Layout** (Spotify dark palette — `#181818`/`#282828` surface, `#1DB954` accent, `#fff` primary text, `#b3b3b3` muted):
- Rounded rectangle (`borderRadius: 12`, subtle shadow), artwork `~56px` rounded on the left.
- Track name (bold) and artist names (muted) — each single-line ellipsis via `whiteSpace: "nowrap"; overflow: "hidden"; textOverflow: "ellipsis"` inside a `minWidth: 0` flex child so truncation actually triggers.
- Place of origin line (muted, small, e.g. `📍 {placeName}`).
- Controls row: play/pause button (icon switches on `track.isPlaying`) + next button. Inline SVG icons for a clean Spotify look (no icon dependency).
- Read-only progress bar: a track `<div>` + filled `<div>` whose width = `displayMs / durationMs * 100%`. **Not a slider — no click/drag handlers**, so it can't seek.
- `controlMessage` rendered as a small muted/generic "Not available" hint when set.

**Interpolation (inside the card, keeps `MapView` clean):**
```js
const anchorRef = useRef({ ms: 0, at: 0 });
const [displayMs, setDisplayMs] = useState(0);
useEffect(() => {                       // re-anchor on each poll / track change
  anchorRef.current = { ms: track.progressMs, at: Date.now() };
  setDisplayMs(track.progressMs ?? 0);
}, [track.progressMs, track.trackId]);
useEffect(() => {                       // tick forward only while playing
  if (!track.isPlaying) return;
  const id = setInterval(() => {
    const { ms, at } = anchorRef.current;
    setDisplayMs(Math.min(ms + (Date.now() - at), track.durationMs ?? ms));
  }, 500);
  return () => clearInterval(id);
}, [track.isPlaying, track.durationMs]);
```

### 3. `src/components/MapView.jsx` — control handlers + render the card

- Import `play`, `pause`, `skipToNext` and `NowPlayingCard`.
- Add `controlMessage` state.
- Refactor the fetch-and-update body of `poll` into a reusable `syncNowPlaying()` (used by both the interval and by controls for an immediate refresh after an action). Keep the existing error classification (`classifyPollError`, refresh/retry) intact for the polling path.
- `handlePlayPause` / `handleNext`: call the matching control fn with `token`; on success clear `controlMessage`, optimistically flip `isPlaying` for instant feedback, then `syncNowPlaying()` to confirm; on `PLAYBACK_UNAVAILABLE` / `NO_ACTIVE_DEVICE` / `SPOTIFY_ERROR:*` set a generic `controlMessage` ("Playback control not available"); on `TOKEN_EXPIRED` reuse `onTokenExpired()`.
- Wrap the render in a positioned container and add the card as a **sibling** of `LeafletMap` (children inside `<MapContainer>` are treated as Leaflet layers, so the card must not go inside it):
```jsx
return (
  <div style={{ position: "relative", height: "100vh", width: "100%" }}>
    <LeafletMap track={track} location={location} />
    {track && (
      <NowPlayingCard
        track={track}
        placeName={location?.placeName}
        onPlayPause={handlePlayPause}
        onNext={handleNext}
        controlMessage={controlMessage}
      />
    )}
  </div>
);
```
The `idle` and `error` returns are unchanged (no track → no card).

### 4. `src/components/AlbumBubble.jsx` — display all artists (small)

`LeafletMap.jsx:34` passes `track.artistName` to the popup. Optionally switch the passed prop to `track.artistNames` so the marker popup also shows all artists. Low priority; keep `artistName` if we'd rather not touch it.

## Tests (Vitest + RTL; coverage gates in `vite.config.js`)

`src/spotify.js` is held to per-file **90 / 75 / 100** — every new function must be covered.

- **`src/__tests__/spotify.test.js`**
  - Update the "returns structured track data" test: mock now includes `is_playing`, `progress_ms`, `item.id`, `item.duration_ms`, multiple `artists`; expected object updated to the widened shape (incl. `artistNames` joined).
  - Update `buildAuthUrl` test to also assert the new scope is present (encoded as `user-read-currently-playing+user-modify-playback-state`).
  - Add tests for `play`/`pause`/`skipToNext`: 204 resolves; 401→`TOKEN_EXPIRED`; 403→`PLAYBACK_UNAVAILABLE`; 404→`NO_ACTIVE_DEVICE`; 429→`RATE_LIMITED:<n>`; other→`SPOTIFY_ERROR:<status>` (covers all branches of `playerCommand`). Mock 204 as `{ status: 204, ok: true, headers: { get: () => null } }`.
- **`src/components/__tests__/NowPlayingCard.test.jsx`** (new): render with a fake track — assert track name, artist names, and place name appear; long strings get an ellipsis style; clicking play/pause calls `onPlayPause` (`getByRole("button", { name: /pause|play/i })`), clicking next calls `onNext`; progress fill renders; render once with `isPlaying: false` and once `true` (fake timers) to cover both interpolation branches; assert `controlMessage` text shows when provided.
- **`src/components/__tests__/MapView.test.jsx`**: mock `NowPlayingCard` (like the existing `LeafletMap` mock) to isolate; update the `fetchCurrentlyPlaying` mock return to include the new fields. Optionally assert a control handler calls the mocked `play`/`pause`.

## Verification

1. `npm test` — all green, coverage thresholds hold (especially `src/spotify.js` per-file 90/75/100).
2. `npx biome check .` — clean (pre-commit hook runs this + tests).
3. Manual end-to-end (`npm start`, Premium account):
   - **Re-login** (scope changed) — approve the new "control playback" permission.
   - Play a track: card appears top-right, artwork/name/artist/origin correct, long names truncate with `…`.
   - Progress bar advances smoothly and re-syncs each poll; pausing freezes it.
   - Play/pause toggles icon + real playback; next advances the track and the map flies to the new artist's origin.
   - With no active device / non-Premium, controls show the generic "not available" hint instead of crashing.

## Out of scope
- Seeking (progress bar is intentionally read-only), previous-track button, volume, device picker.
- Reducing the 5s poll interval (interpolation + post-action refresh cover responsiveness).

